INT. REFRIGERATED DELIVERY TRUCK - CARGO BAY - NIGHT

Frost on the walls. Crates of frozen fish and one steel case chained to the floor. Four people crouch in the cold, their breath hanging in the weak red work light.

LEOPOLDO "POLO" REYES (50s, ski cap) is working the case's lock with a pick. NADIA FARRAH (30s, hooded parka) holds a flashlight. MAEVE DUNLEAVY (20s, driver's gloves) watches a phone. HIDEKI OTA (40s, quiet, a thermal bag at his hip) counts seconds under his breath.

                    POLO
          Hold it steady.

                    NADIA
          I am holding it steady.

                    MAEVE
          Two minutes to the checkpoint.

                    HIDEKI
          Ninety seconds. Maybe.

                    POLO
          Quiet, I'm listening for the tumblers.

                    NADIA
          You can't hear tumblers in a freezer, Polo.

                    MAEVE
          He's hearing something.

                    HIDEKI
          Sixty seconds.

He taps his wrist. She flinches. He doesn't. The lock gives with a small, sweet click.

                    POLO
          Got it.

                    NADIA
          Open it.

                    MAEVE
          Thirty seconds, open it!

He lifts the lid. Nobody breathes. Inside, a velvet tray holds six lumpy brown bundles. He peels one open: a salted cod.

                    HIDEKI
          It's fish.

                    POLO
          It's all fish.

Nadia swears under her breath. Maeve laughs once, high and brittle. The truck slows. Brakes hiss. Somewhere outside, a guard's voice calls a greeting.
